  "body": "The native `post` command accepts two short counterclockwise arcs and writes two G03 blocks with coincident start and end XY coordinates. Both blocks have a nonzero center offset. A control that treats these blocks as full circles can cut a circle instead of a short stroke.\n\nI reproduced this with CamCraft `post 0.25.0 (boa_engine)` and the original `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`. The post, CL reader and post script match main at `b44a422bb`. I checked the generated file. No controller or machine ran it.\n\n## Reproduce\n\nSave the following synthetic input as `tiny.cnc`. The coordinates in the intermediate file use micrometres.\n\n```\n; HSMW-CNC v1\nPARAM OperationName Arc precision witness\nPARAM SpindleSpeed 6000\nPARAM WorkOffset 1\nPARAM OriginX 0\nPARAM OriginY 0\nPARAM OriginZ 0\nPARAM ToolDiameter 4\nPARAM ClearancePlane 18\nPARAM RetractPlane 18\nPARAM TopOfStock 6\nTOOL 1 EM-0400-2FL\nSECTION Arc precision witness\nRapid X 18123 Y 5432 Z 18000\nPlunge X 18123 Y 5432 Z 5500 F 45000\nArc CCW X 18123 Y 5433 Z 5500 F 180000 I 10123 J 5432\nArc CCW X 18123 Y 5434 Z 5500 F 180000 I 10123 J 5432\nRapid X 18123 Y 5434 Z 18000\nENDSECTION\n```\n\nRun `cargo run -p camcraft-post --bin post -- --units inch assets/posts/fanuc.cps tiny.cnc tiny.nc`.\n\nThe input Y positions are 5432, 5433 and 5434 µm. Each arc has a sweep of about 0.00716°. In the NC file, the preceding position and both arc endpoints are X0.7135 Y0.2139. Each arc reads:\n\n```text\nG03 X0.7135 Y0.2139 Z0.2165 I-0.315 J0. F7.09\n```\n\nThe command exited successfully. It reported 13 mapped records, nine blocks and zero swallowed records.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe post must preserve the short motion at the selected precision or refuse it with a diagnostic. It must distinguish a short arc from an intended full turn. Pin this input through the native post command. Also check a representable short arc and a genuine full circle.\n\nFound while testing #1869. A check in the new sketch generator protects that feature. The native post also accepts intermediate files from other sources. #2191 concerned the radius-word mode and a different rounding failure.\n\nSuggested labels are `bug`, `P1`, `area:post`, `effort:high`, and `source:agent`.\n",
